.TH DWG2DXF 1 "2026-10-15" "version 1.0"
.SH NAME
dwg2dxf \- Conversor from dwg/dxf to dxf
.SH SYNOPSIS
dwg2dxf <input> [-b] <-version> <output>
.br
dwg2dxf <input> -o <output> [-version] [-b] [-y]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwg2dxf is a console converter from DWG/DXF to DXF. Either input format can
be converted to another DXF version.
.PP
DXF input passes a source-text admission gate before output creation or
replacement. Observed malformed/undefined input, discarded/replaced text,
unrepresented escapes and ambiguous non-ASCII legacy decoding cause a nonzero
exit. Legacy UTF8/UTF16 declarations are not admitted merely because their
names are recognized. Later metadata or a full advisory list cannot erase
earlier observed loss. ASCII and represented CIF/MIF with unknown page metadata,
and valid modern UTF8 with inert legacy metadata, remain eligible. Unknown source
revision is not invented; only decoder-independent text is eligible without it.
.PP
This is a necessary source-text gate, not whole-drawing, charset-mapping,
DWG or native-consumer qualification. Existing structural/owner
and unsupported-record checks still apply. Ordinary library reads and default
adapter exports retain their tolerant behavior; no automatic recovery is added.
.PP
For both DWG and DXF input, required semantic output text also passes a separate
lossless target-transport gate. Invalid UTF8, unsupported supplementary-character
downgrade, unsafe record framing and high-byte opaque text without qualified
source provenance cause a nonzero exit without publishing or replacing output.
Modern UTF8 and qualified legacy BMP/codepage/CIF transport remain available.
Literal escape-looking semantic backslashes are selectively quoted; MTEXT
formatting and raw binary/handle roles are not globally rewritten. This is not
complete charset, raw-application-data, native-rendering or DWG support
qualification. Ordinary library writers default to Compatible; the CLI explicitly
opts into RequireLossless without an additional command-line switch.
.SH OPTIONS
input      existing file to convert
   -b         optional, sets output as binary dxf
   -B         optional, batch mode reads a text file whit a list of full path input
               files and saves with the same name in the indicated folder as output
   -y -Y      optional, Warning! if output dxf exist overwrite without ask
   -d -D      optional, enables debug tracing
   -version   version output of dxf file (required by the positional form,
              optional with -o; otherwise the source revision is retained)
   output     output file name

The -o form is compatible with FreeCAD's external DWG converter invocation.
It writes ASCII DXF unless -b is specified and does not prompt. If the output
already exists, conversion fails unless -y is specified. AC1012/R13 input is
written as AC1014/R14 because AC1012 is not a supported output revision.
.PP
Batch mode requires an explicit output version and an existing output
directory. Its regular-file list accepts LF, CRLF and a final line without a
newline. Empty lines are ignored; filename spaces and UTF-8 bytes are retained.
The limits are 128 KiB per filename, 16 MiB of physical list bytes and 10000
inputs. Invalid lists or identity collisions reject before conversion. Batch
mode never prompts: replacing an existing destination requires -y or -Y.
Independent items continue after ordinary conversion failures, but the process
returns nonzero if any item fails. Each file is published atomically; a failed
batch does not roll back files already converted successfully.
.PP
Install dwg2dxf and either place its bindir first on FreeCAD's PATH or select
the LibreDWG-compatible converter in FreeCAD's DWG preferences and configure
the full executable path. In automatic mode FreeCAD may try another converter
after failure. A successful conversion means that DXF was produced; FreeCAD's
DXF importer may still not support every preserved entity or 3D feature.
.PP
The end-to-end profile qualified by this project is FreeCAD 1.1.3 on macOS 27
arm64 with the C++ DXF importer, using the installed converter for a generated
AC1015 nonzero-Z LINE through both open and insert. Both Automatic
(DWGConversion=0) and LibreDWG-only (DWGConversion=1) modes were checked with
PATH discovery; the Automatic-mode control selected this executable first and
did not run ODA/QCAD fallback. Automatic mode may still try another converter
after failure. Native Linux and Windows profiles are not yet qualified; entity
and version support remains specific to the published support matrix.
.PP
This package supplies the DWG-to-DXF import-side program for FreeCAD Draft's
importDWG.open() and importDWG.insert() workflows only; it does not include
FreeCAD's paired dxf2dwg program and does not provide LibreDWG-based DWG
export. FreeCAD shares its TeighaFileConverter preference between import and
export. If that preference names dwg2dxf, FreeCAD derives the sibling
dxf2dwg path for export; when the sibling is missing, the current resolver
does not fall back to PATH. To discover dwg2dxf from PATH without replacing a
separate export setup, do not set the shared preference to either LibreDWG
executable. If you configure this dwg2dxf path directly, route export through
a separate converter that actually provides dxf2dwg.

     version can be:
        -R12   dxf release 12 version
        -v2000 dxf version 2000
        -v2004 dxf version 2004
        -v2007 dxf version 2007
        -v2010 dxf version 2010
